Description: CVE-2026-118380 - Properly verify RPCSEC_GSS call arguments
 In the RPCSEC_GSS server (svc_auth_gss.c), the sequence window state and
 the protection service level (none/integrity/privacy) were taken from the
 call credential before the verifier was checked, and the service level
 from the context-establishment request (which is not integrity-protected)
 was retained.  Add svcauth_gss_check_call() which checks the context,
 sequence window and verifier first, then updates the sequence state and
 takes the service level from the verified credential.  Also adds an
 RPCSEC_GSS service-level regression test to the rpc unit tests.
 Backported from upstream; the test hunks were hand-ported to the
 K&R-style test sources of this version.
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/krb5/krb5/commit/2cda39a6c0a2ee19b7cdd811e07d564506388fe3
Author: Greg Hudson <ghudson@mit.edu>
Last-Update: 2026-11-17
