+success('CVE-2026-107364 regression test')
Description: CVE-2026-112316 - Free partial tl-data on XDR decode failure
 In xdr_krb5_tl_data(), when decoding fails part-way through the list
 (or an allocation fails), the already-decoded tl-data entries and the
 entry currently being decoded were leaked.  Route all failure paths in
 the XDR_DECODE case through a decode_fail label which frees both lists.
 .
 Backported from upstream; the xdr_bytes() maximum length argument is
 kept as ~0 to match krb5 1.20.1 (GSSRPC_MAX_ELEMENT_SIZE is not
 present in this version).
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/krb5/krb5/commit/fe0a8a67f2fce89bb9d62031219a1f5a064c4df1
Author: Julien Rische <jrische@redhat.com>
Last-Update: 2026-11-17
---
--- a/src/lib/kadm5/kadm_rpc_xdr.c
+++ b/src/lib/kadm5/kadm_rpc_xdr.c
@@ -301,7 +301,7 @@
 
